    "Last changed 31 October 2026.",
    "# In short",
    "wrela.dev is free. It shows no ads, sells nothing, and never sells or rents anything about you to anyone.",
    "We built accounts to know as little about you as we can. We don't ask for your email, your name, your age or where you are. We never see a password. We don't show ads and we don't use anyone else's analytics.",
    "You can play every game without an account. Then nothing about you leaves your device.",
    "# What we keep, and only this",
    "- An account number and an account handle, which are random numbers we make. Your passkey knows your account by its handle.",
    "- Your passkey's public key, its credential ID, its signature counter, and when it was added and last used. The private key never leaves your device, and we never see it.",
    "- Your account's name, kept as four numbers that pick words from our lists. You never type it.",
    "- Your recovery codes, only as fingerprints (SHA-256 hashes), so a copy of our records can't be used to sign in.",
    "- One session cookie, which keeps you signed in. Your browser keeps it for wrela.dev and sends it only there. No script can read it, ours included. Our server keeps its fingerprint, with when the session began and was last seen. Games never see it. While you sign in or add a passkey, a second cookie holds that sign-in's token for at most five minutes. We use no other cookies.",
    "- A short-lived token for each game you play while signed in, which can only submit runs. We keep its fingerprint for an hour.",
    "- Your runs. Each is the buttons you pressed, tick by tick (a replay), the time and category our server works out from them, and when you posted it. Anyone can fetch a posted run's replay by its fingerprint (its SHA-256), which the boards show.",
    "- What you agreed to. That's which version of these terms and this policy, that you said you're 13 or older, and when. Once you agree to what posting makes public, it's also which version and when, and whether you chose \"Post my best runs\".",
    "- How many runs you uploaded in the past hour, and fingerprints of the replays you uploaded, to stop the same run being sent twice.",
    "- Times on our server's own clock, for when each of these was made.",
    "# What we never keep",
    "- No email address, phone number, real name or typed name of any kind.",
    "- No password.",
    "- No chat, messages or other free text.",
    "- No photos, voice or video.",
    "- No location.",
    "- No IP addresses. Our server program is never told your IP address. Cloudflare (below) sees it, as any host must, to deliver each request. Our Worker uses it for one thing only. It counts each address's requests over a minute, to limit how fast anyone can try to sign in. Your IP address is never written down or logged.",
    "- No third-party analytics, advertising, tracking pixels or social buttons.",
    "# What we use identifiers for",
    "The account number, the account handle, the passkey's credential ID and the session and game tokens are persistent identifiers. We use them only to:",
    "- sign you in, keep you signed in, and let you sign out or end a session elsewhere;",
    "- show your verified runs on the leaderboards under your account's name;",
    "- check uploaded runs, enforce the upload limits, and stop cheating and abuse;",
    "- keep the service secure and working, and find and fix its faults;",
