    "We never use them to show ads, to build a profile of you, to follow you across other sites, or to contact you.",
    "# Lines we don't cross",
    "Each of these would mean collecting personal information. That would need a new design and, for children, a parent's verified consent first. We won't do any of them without changing this policy first:",
    "- asking for an email address or a phone number;",
    "- letting anyone type a name, a message or anything else;",
    "- chat, voice or video, including video of runs;",
    "- precise location;",
    "- third-party analytics, ads or social sign-in;",
    "- using an identifier for anything beyond the list above;",
    "- keeping IP addresses.",
    "# Who helps us run it",
    "- Cloudflare serves the website and runs our server, and stores its records and their backups. It sees the IP address of each visit and connection, as any web host does.",
    "- GitHub holds the source code. It never receives account data.",
    "Each acts on our behalf, and none of them gets your account's records to use for itself.",
    "# How long we keep it",
    "We keep your account's records until you delete the account. A session ends after 90 days, or when you sign out or end it. A game's token ends after an hour. When you delete your account, its records go from our server right away, from Cloudflare's caches of the public boards within five minutes, and from the backups within [30 days: to be set with the backup's retention]. A posted run's replay never changes, so Cloudflare's caches may keep a copy fetched by its fingerprint for up to a year after the account is deleted, even though our server no longer has it.",
    "# Your choices",
    "- Export. Choose Account, then Export my data, to get everything above as a JSON file.",
    "- Delete. Choose Account, then Delete account, to delete your passkeys' records, sessions, recovery codes, runs and name right away. We'll ask you to sign in with your passkey first.",
